% You are an expert TypeScript engineer. Implement the Render Workflows adapter behind SiteVelocity's workflow port.

<include>prompts/context/sitevelocity-preamble.prompt</include>

<pdd-reason>Dispatch and observe durable research work without leaking Render transport details into the domain.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[{"name":"createRenderWorkflowAdapter","signature":"(transport: RenderWorkflowTransport, config: RenderWorkflowConfig) -> WorkflowEngine","returns":"WorkflowEngine"}]}}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Map provider-neutral workflow commands and statuses to a bounded Render transport with idempotency and sanitized failures.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- DOES NOT implement research tasks, domain logic, persistence, or deployment provisioning.
- MUST NOT expose Render SDK or HTTP types through `WorkflowEngine`.
- MUST NOT log or return API keys, authorization headers, or request bodies containing secrets.
- DOES NOT retry beyond the declared transport policy.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
workflow command: a provider-neutral task name, command identifier, payload reference, and correlation metadata.
accepted dispatch: Render acknowledged one durable execution and returned a provider run identifier.
idempotent dispatch: repeating one command identifier does not create another execution.
sanitized failure: a stable failure code without raw provider content or credentials.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Validate configuration and commands before any transport call.
R2 (MUST): Send exactly one declared task slug and command identifier per dispatch.
R3 (MUST): Preserve correlation, site, plan-version, and command identifiers through status results.
R4 (MUST): Return the same accepted execution for repeated identical command identifiers and reject different-input reuse.
R5 (MUST): Map provider states into queued, running, succeeded, failed, or cancelled without inventing completion.
R6 (MUST): Bound status calls and retries by caller configuration and expose rate limiting separately from authentication and provider failure.
R7 (MUST NOT): Return provider response bodies, SDK values, secrets, or internal URLs.
R8 (MUST): Convert unknown provider states into a sanitized provider_unrecognized_state failure rather than success.
</contract_rules>

<deliverables>
Generate `lib/adapters/render/workflow-engine.ts` exporting `createRenderWorkflowAdapter` and provider-neutral port types.
</deliverables>
